\name{asmBUSCOcheck}
\alias{asmBUSCOcheck}
\title{
asmBUSCOcheck
}
\description{
%%  Determine if there are BUSCO genes missing in the main assembly that are
%%  are found in the alternate assembly. BUSCO should be run on two sister
%%  assemblies—that is they should be output from a single set of reads from the
%%  same genome assembler as main and alternate assemblies OR output from a
%%  haplotig/duplicate contig purging program such as purge_haplotigs or
%%  purge_dups. Function requires two BUSCO (or compleasm) full_table.tsv files.
}
\usage{
asmBUSCOcheck(asm1.busco = NULL, asm2.busco = NULL, summary = FALSE, out = NULL)
}
%- maybe also 'usage' for other objects documented here.
\arguments{
  \item{asm1.busco}{
%%     BUSCO or compleasm full_table.tsv output for the main/primary assembly (required)
}
  \item{asm2.busco}{
%%     BUSCO or compleasm full_table.tsv output for the alternate assembly (required)
}
  \item{summary}{
%%     Summarise the number of BUSCOs found on each alternate assembly contigs
%%     that should be kept (optional)
}
  \item{out}{
%%     File prefix for output file. Will be in the form [prefix].txt (optional)
}
}
\details{
%%  Given two BUSCO full table outputs, this function will identify whether or
%%  not there are BUSCOs missing in the primary/main assembly that are found in
%%  the alternate assembly. The full_table.tsv can be from either BUSCO or compleasm.
%%  The function will list the contig names of the alternate assembly that contains
%%  "missing" BUSCOs from the primary assembly. This list of contigs names can
%%  by used to subset the alternate assembly using a program like seqtk subseq
%%  to isolate the contigs in question, which can then be added back to the main
%%  assembly. Future development should include identifying BUSCOs
%%
}
\value{
%%  \keep {list of contigs from asm2 that contain BUSCOs that are "missing" in asm1}
%%  \summary {summary of BUSCOs that are located on the contigs in 'keep'}
%% ...
}
\references{
%% https://busco.ezlab.org/
%% https://github.com/huangnengCSU/compleasm
%% https://github.com/lh3/seqtk
}
\author{
%%  Gen Morinaga
}
\note{
%%  This function outputs a list of names. It takes as arguments tab-delimited
%%  data tables. It makes no attempt to fasta files.
}


